+Periods are ISO-8601 strings in UTC on a whole hour, such as `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z`. A rental of a day or more
+starts and ends at midnight UTC. `end` is the start of the day after the last rented day, so one day is
+`start: 2026-07-01T00:00:00Z, end: 2026-07-02T00:00:00Z`. Money is always an integer number of euro cents.
+Quoting or booking an unknown item throws. So does a period that is not a whole number of hours, a rental of a
+day or more that does not start and end at midnight UTC, and an hourly rental of an item without an hourly price.
+Booking also throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period.
+
+Periods are half-open, so a booking ending on 3 July does not block one starting on 3 July, and a booking ending
+at 12:00 does not block one starting at 12:00. Cancellations are not implemented yet; the cancellation policy
+will be added later.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
